+---
+name: setup-website-apollo-declarative-backend
+description: "Configure or resume a derived backend app website: branding, localized policies, store/app links, invitations, deletion, optional GA4 and release handoffs."
+---
+
+# Setup Backend Website
+
+Use the active backend project and its own `scripts/setup_project.py`; read `ai_development/backend_setup.md` first. Receive the confirmed project identity, environment and shared configuration from root setup, or inspect them when invoked directly. Reuse confirmed choices, ask only for missing decisions, and preserve deferred/declined choices unless the developer changes them. Do not rerun unrelated root or feature setup.
+
+Inspect `ai_development/project_setup.json`, relevant nonsecret configuration and existing feature records. Keep the CLI's `managed_environment`, `planned_integrations`, secret references and completion fields intact. After an authorized setup apply, merge only this feature's entry under `feature_setup` using the record contract in backend_setup.md. Preview-only work must not write the record. Return actual configuration, verification and pending actions to root setup; never equate configuration with deployment or live acceptance.
+
+Read ai_development/backend_website_spec.md. Reuse website/site.json choices; collect app name/logo/screenshots/text, operator/support contact, exact domain/root/www hosts, locales and translated UI/privacy/terms/support/deletion content. Establish actual data practices/providers/retention and a working deletion request process; sample text remains draft. Collect real store URLs or coming-soon state, Apple App ID prefix/bundle IDs, Android package/release or Play App Signing fingerprints and supported HTTP link paths. Native entitlements/intent filters/push remain a frontend handoff, never edits to the frontend setup skill.
+
+For GA4 collect/reuse enabled state, web measurement ID, optional property/data-stream IDs, domain/locales, events, campaign/ad allowlist, iOS campaign/Play referrer mappings, consent/privacy choice, owned cross-domain hosts and debug acceptance. Confirm Enhanced Measurement is disabled before tag activation. No browser-tag API key is needed; server Measurement Protocol is unimplemented. Invitation/share pages never load analytics. Explain configured versus actual GA4 report verification.
+
+Collect the owning invitation/share preview service or fixed read-only preview_url/public fields; absent wiring reports unavailable. Never invent business success or log capability tokens. Configure actual deletion_url or monitored support-email process rather than a fake submit action. Keep public profile/assets separate from all credentials.
+
+Use setup_project.py --website-config and optional --website-assets with WEBSITE_ENABLED=true: preview, inspect, apply. Preserve local conflicts with intended resolution/--keep-local; use versioned image names for asset updates. Setup does not publish/contact providers/deploy. Production needs reviewed nondraft content. verify_website.py probes public/profile/association contracts; native-device, live invitation/deletion and GA4 checks remain separate. Deployment selects the same-image website service and removes only it when disabled. Preserve per-project/API/ACME routing; no live domain/server changes are implied by setup.
+
+## Resumable website setup
+
+Use `feature_setup.website` for the choice and status summary; `website/site.json` remains the public runtime profile. Record only nonsecret readiness and remaining actions, including profile path, configured hosts/locales, draft versus reviewed content, store/association readiness, frontend handoff, invitation/deletion service readiness and optional analytics verification. Do not duplicate the public profile or copy invitation tokens into the record. Offer analytics independently of the website; deferring GA4 must not block a draft website. Retain that subchoice under feature_setup.website.analytics with choice (enabled/deferred/declined), configuration, verification and pending_actions using the same status contract. Do not copy private analytics identifiers or report collection verified from configuration alone.
+
+For a new derived project, complete the root foundation first and use its own CLI thereafter. Example from the active project (omit assets when not needed):
+
+```sh
+python3 scripts/setup_project.py --set WEBSITE_ENABLED=true --website-config /absolute/public-site.json --website-assets /absolute/public-images
+python3 scripts/setup_project.py --set WEBSITE_ENABLED=true --website-config /absolute/public-site.json --website-assets /absolute/public-images --apply
+```
+
+Before changing an enabled production profile, establish whether the developer requests draft configuration, release preparation or publication. Keep drafts off the public production runtime. The CLI rejects an enabled draft with ENVIRONMENT=production; never change the existing production environment to evade that guard. Identify the project's separate draft-preview target/workflow before applying, or retain that handoff as pending if none exists. Hand accepted server/domain work to configure-server-apollo-declarative-backend and publication/restart to deploy-and-restart-apollo-declarative-backend; setup alone performs neither. Use the owning project's existing release workflow for the separately managed draft preview; do not assume an API deployment updates it.
+
+Report separately: template available, profile written, website deployed, public HTTPS verified, and per-app release acceptance. Real approved policies/deletion handling, store listings, native identifiers/device association, invitation service and optional GA4 collection are derived-project acceptance inputs. Never mark them passed from fixtures or empty association files. Return concrete unresolved inputs and frontend/native handoff requirements.
