+
+## Feature setup delegation and progress
+
+`setup-apollo-declarative-backend` owns the foundation and optional deployment target. It discovers accepted/enabled feature setup skills in the active project's `.agents/skills`; identity, AI, memory, knowledge and website own their own parameters and verification. Feature-specific requests can invoke their skill directly. New derived bundles include all `setup-*-apollo-declarative-backend` skill directories, so delegation needs no framework checkout. Existing skill directories are preserved on reruns; use the normal selective update workflow to adopt new skill revisions.
+
+Read existing managed settings, `planned_integrations`, feature records and public website profile before asking for answers. Default disabled settings are not explicit declines. Preserve confirmed deferred/declined choices, resolve conflicts with enabled runtime settings explicitly, and resume unfinished accepted features even when `setup_complete` is already true.
+
+Feature skills merge their own entry under the additive `feature_setup` object in `ai_development/project_setup.json` after an authorized apply. The setup CLI preserves this object as an unknown record field; it does not synthesize feature choices or change verification states. Preserve all sibling features and CLI-owned fields. Use feature keys `identity`, `ai`, `memory`, `knowledge`, `website`, or a discovered feature's declared key. Record:
+
+- `choice`: `enabled`, `deferred` or `declined`; absent/null means unresolved. An enabled choice records intent, not successful activation.
+- `configuration`: `not_started`, `planned` or `configured` based on actual results.
+- `deployment`: `not_requested`, `pending` or `verified`, separately from configuration.
+- `verification`: an object of named checks with `not_run`, `passed`, `failed` or `deferred` and nonsecret evidence references.
+- `pending_actions`: concrete missing inputs/access, manual handoffs or unverified steps.
+
+Keep confirmed feature-specific nonsecret choices/readiness under the same entry as needed; keep actual runtime values in the CLI-owned environment/public profile and existing AI behavior record. Never store raw credentials, sessions, identity tokens, invitation capabilities or private documents here. Reread and merge the latest record before an atomic write; never replace it with a frontend schema. Preview-only requests perform no record writes. Explicit decisions to defer/decline can be retained when setup progress recording is requested, without enabling an integration or overwriting its prior runtime settings.
+
+Website setup is owned by [setup-website-apollo-declarative-backend](../.agents/skills/setup-website-apollo-declarative-backend/SKILL.md). It collects branding/locales, approved policies and deletion handling, store and association identities, dynamic preview wiring, optional analytics and native release handoffs. Template availability, configured draft, deployed site, public HTTPS checks and per-app release acceptance are distinct outcomes. Do not require production store accounts or enable analytics merely to configure a draft.
